.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PATINA-MENU 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-menu
.Nd the Patina desktop's menu, and menus for the other pieces
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -at Ar x , Ns Ar y
.Nm
.Op Fl -at Ar x , Ns Ar y
.Op Fl -edge Cm top | bottom | left | right
.Fl -item Ar id Ns = Ns Ar label
.Op Fl -item Ar id Ns = Ns Ar label | Fl -separator ...
.Nm
.Fl -tooltip Ar text
.Op Fl -at Ar x , Ns Ar y
.Op Fl -edge Cm top | bottom | left | right
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the menu a right click on the empty desktop opens.
.Xr patina-compositor 1
runs it, as its
.Ic desktop_menu ,
at the pointer.
.Pp
It offers the style, Default, Light or Dark, set through
.Xr gsettings 1
as GNOME's
.Ic color-scheme :
apps that follow it change at once.
The skin is chosen in
.Xr patina-settings 1 .
Below are Wallpaper\&..., which opens
.Xr patina-settings 1
at its Wallpaper page; items to copy the built-in skins to the bar's skins
folder, to open that folder, and to open the bar's config file; Process Manager,
which brings it forward or starts it, as Ctrl+Shift+Escape does; and
Settings\&....
A click elsewhere, Escape, or losing the keyboard closes it.
.Pp
Settings and the process manager are started by the compositor, so they're listed on its Processes
page; outside Patina's compositor the menu starts it itself.
.Pp
Given items,
.Nm
is instead a menu of them, for a piece too small to hold its own menu, as
.Xr patina-hud 1
is: a window tab's right click opens New Window and Close Window this way,
so the menu isn't cut off at the bar's edge.
It shows the items in order, prints the
.Ar id
of the one chosen on its standard output and exits; closed without a
choice, it prints nothing.
It wears the bar's skin.
.Pp
With
.Fl -tooltip ,
.Nm
is a tooltip saying
.Ar text ,
centred on
.Ar x
past
.Ar y ,
for the bar's tooltips: it takes no clicks or keys, and goes when its
standard input closes, so whatever started it ends it by closing the pipe,
or by ending.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -at Ar x , Ns Ar y
Where to open, in the screen's logical pixels; the top-left corner
without it.
.It Fl -edge Cm top | bottom | left | right
Which screen edge
.Ar y
counts from: with
.Cm bottom ,
from the bottom, and the menu opens upward from there, as from a bar at the
bottom.
With
.Cm left
or
.Cm right ,
.Ar x
counts from that edge instead, and the menu opens out to the side, as from
a split bar's column there.
.Cm top
by default.
.It Fl -item Ar id Ns = Ns Ar label
An item saying
.Ar label ,
which prints
.Ar id
when chosen; without a label, it says
.Ar id .
.It Fl -separator
A line between items.
.It Fl -tooltip Ar text
Show
.Ar text
as a tooltip until standard input closes.
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-hud/config.toml
Where the skin is written.
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-hud/skins/
Skins of your own.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A menu above a bar at the bottom, 300 pixels in:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
patina-menu --at 300,45 --edge bottom \
    --item new-window='New Window' --item close='Close Window'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-hud 1 ,
.Xr patina-settings 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
